{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q4gjYXwNLULJcXopChgDTX","type":"tool_result","content":"60\tTolerance (all five): `max_atol=1e-5`, `max_rtol=0.05`. Smallest workload (24 group-tiles /\n61\t96 head-tiles) is the occupancy-risk case for any grid-shrinking optimization; largest (896\n62\thead-tiles ≈ 2–8 waves on 108 SMs) is the throughput case.\n63\t\n64\t---\n65\t\n66\t## 2. Candidate lineage strategy\n67\t\n68\t**One variable per candidate.** Each ID changes exactly one axis vs. its parent so any\n69\tcorrectness or speed delta is attributable. Lineage is a **greedy chain**: the accepted best so\n70\tfar is the parent of the next probe; rejected probes do not become parents. Config/tile/precision\n71\tknobs baked into the kernel source are treated as source changes ⇒ new IDs (no autotuner that\n72\twould make \"one immutable kernel\" ambiguous across workloads).\n73\t\n74\tPlanned spine (each step gated on the previous passing correctness; exact later IDs depend on\n75\toutcomes — this is the priority order, not a promise of count):\n76\t\n77\t- **c001 — correctness anchor (per-`(b,c,h)`).** Grid `B·C·32`; faithful mapping of §1. fp32\n78\t  accumulators, exp-of-difference, no max-subtraction, bf16 cast only at store + matmul-2\n79\t  operands. `num_warps=8`, `num_stages=2–3`. Goal: **pass all 5**, establish baseline geomean.\n80\t  Nothing else matters until this is green.\n81\t- **c002 — per-group `G` fusion.** One program per `(b,c,g)` computes `G=Cmat@Bmatᵀ` once, loops\n82\t  the 4 heads: `M_h=G∘L_h`, `Y_h=M_h@X_h`. Cuts matmul-1 and B/C loads 4×; grid → `B·C·8`.\n83\t  Hypothesis: net win from reduced compute/traffic; **watch occupancy on (1,3)=24 tiles**.\n84\t- **c003 — matmul-2 precision knob.** If c001/c002 pass comfortably, keep bf16 tensor-core\n85\t  (fast). Only if any workload is marginal/fails, branch a candidate with fp32/TF32 matmul-2 as\n86\t  a correctness-preserving fallback. (Precision is a correctness lever first, perf second.)\n87\t- **c004 — KV tiling + causal skip (no renorm).** `BLOCK_M`∈{64,128}, kv loop in blocks with\n88\t  strict-upper-triangular block skip; `i≥j` mask only on the diagonal block. Lowers register\n89\t  pressure and skips ~half the score work. Compare vs full-128."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"186381ab-5278-4fc8-9646-c8c71e3836fb","uuid":"719a6309-6e26-408e-aeb4-8e11b5301df1","timestamp":"2026-09-16T17:51:19.481Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L1-070_mamba2_fused_intra_chunk_diagonal_computation/docs/plan.md","content":"Tolerance (all five): `max_atol=1e-5`, `max_rtol=0.05`. Smallest workload (24 group-tiles /\n96 head-tiles) is the occupancy-risk case for any grid-shrinking optimization; largest (896\nhead-tiles ≈ 2–8 waves on 108 SMs) is the throughput case.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Candidate lineage strategy\n\n**One variable per candidate.** Each ID changes exactly one axis vs. its parent so any\ncorrectness or speed delta is attributable. Lineage is a **greedy chain**: the accepted best so\nfar is the parent of the next probe; rejected probes do not become parents. Config/tile/precision\nknobs baked into the kernel source are treated as source changes ⇒ new IDs (no autotuner that\nwould make \"one immutable kernel\" ambiguous across workloads).\n\nPlanned spine (each step gated on the previous passing correctness; exact later IDs depend on\noutcomes — this is the priority order, not a promise of count):\n\n- **c001 — correctness anchor (per-`(b,c,h)`).** Grid `B·C·32`; faithful mapping of §1. fp32\n  accumulators, exp-of-difference, no max-subtraction, bf16 cast only at store + matmul-2\n  operands. `num_warps=8`, `num_stages=2–3`. Goal: **pass all 5**, establish baseline geomean.\n  Nothing else matters until this is green.\n- **c002 — per-group `G` fusion.** One program per `(b,c,g)` computes `G=Cmat@Bmatᵀ` once, loops\n  the 4 heads: `M_h=G∘L_h`, `Y_h=M_h@X_h`. Cuts matmul-1 and B/C loads 4×; grid → `B·C·8`.\n  Hypothesis: net win from reduced compute/traffic; **watch occupancy on (1,3)=24 tiles**.\n- **c003 — matmul-2 precision knob.** If c001/c002 pass comfortably, keep bf16 tensor-core\n  (fast). Only if any workload is marginal/fails, branch a candidate with fp32/TF32 matmul-2 as\n  a correctness-preserving fallback. (Precision is a correctness lever first, perf second.)\n- **c004 — KV tiling + causal skip (no renorm).** `BLOCK_M`∈{64,128}, kv loop in blocks with\n  strict-upper-triangular block skip; `i≥j` mask only on the diagonal block. Lowers register\n  pressure and skips ~half the score work. Compare vs full-128.","numLines":30,"startLine":60,"totalLines":260}}}
